.IX Title "Encode::ISO2022 3"
.TH Encode::ISO2022 3 "2013-09-23" "perl v5.34.0" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
Encode::ISO2022 \- ISO/IEC 2022 character encoding scheme
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 2
\&  package FooEncoding;
\&  use base qw(Encode::ISO2022);
\&  
\&  _\|_PACKAGE_\|_\->Define(
\&    Name => \*(Aqfoo\-encoding\*(Aq,
\&    CCS => [ {...CCS one...}, {...CCS two...}, ....]
\&  );
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This module provides a character encoding scheme (\s-1CES\s0) switching a set of
multiple coded character sets (\s-1CCS\s0).
.PP
A class method \fBDefine()\fR may take following arguments.
.IP "Alias => \s-1REGEX\s0" 4
.IX Item "Alias => REGEX"
The regular expression representing alias of this encoding, if any.
.IP "Name => \s-1STRING\s0" 4
.IX Item "Name => STRING"
The name of this encoding as Encode::Encoding object.
Mandatory.
.IP "\s-1CCS\s0 => [ \s-1FEATURE, FEATURE, ...\s0]" 4
.IX Item "CCS => [ FEATURE, FEATURE, ...]"
List of features defining CCSs used by this encoding.
Mandatory.
Each item is a hash reference containing following items.
.RS 4
.IP "bytes => \s-1NUMBER\s0" 4
.IX Item "bytes => NUMBER"
Number of bytes to represent each character.
Default is 1.
.IP "cl => \s-1BOOLEAN\s0" 4
.IX Item "cl => BOOLEAN"
If true value is set, this \s-1CCS\s0 includes map to/from code points between
0/0 and 1/15.
There should be one \s-1CCS\s0 with this flag to reset broken designation.
.IP "dec_only => \s-1BOOLEAN\s0" 4
.IX Item "dec_only => BOOLEAN"
If true value is set, this \s-1CCS\s0 will be used only for decoding.
.IP "encoding => \s-1STRING\s0 | \s-1ENCODING\s0" 4
.IX Item "encoding => STRING | ENCODING"
Encode::Encoding object used as \s-1CCS,\s0 or its name.
Mandatory.
.Sp
Encodings used for \s-1CCS\s0 must provide \*(L"raw\*(R" conversion.
Namely, they must be stateless and fixed-length conversion over 94^n or 96^n
code tables.
Encode::ISO2022::CCS lists available CCSs.
.IP "g => \s-1STRING\s0" 4
.IX Item "g => STRING"
.PD 0
.IP "g_init => \s-1STRING\s0" 4
.IX Item "g_init => STRING"
.PD
Working set this \s-1CCS\s0 may be designated to:
\&\f(CW\*(Aqg0\*(Aq\fR, \f(CW\*(Aqg1\*(Aq\fR, \f(CW\*(Aqg2\*(Aq\fR or \f(CW\*(Aqg3\*(Aq\fR.
.Sp
If \f(CW\*(C`g_init\*(C'\fR is set, this \s-1CCS\s0 will be designated at beginning of coversion
implicitly, and at end of conversion explicitly.
.Sp
If \f(CW\*(C`g\*(C'\fR or \f(CW\*(C`g_init\*(C'\fR is set and neither of \f(CW\*(C`ls\*(C'\fR nor \f(CW\*(C`ss\*(C'\fR is set,
this \s-1CCS\s0 will be invoked when it is designated.
.Sp
If neither of \f(CW\*(C`g\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`g_init\*(C'\fR, \f(CW\*(C`ls\*(C'\fR nor \f(CW\*(C`ss\*(C'\fR is set,
this \s-1CCS\s0 is invoked always.
.IP "g_seq => \s-1STRING\s0" 4
.IX Item "g_seq => STRING"
Escape sequence to designate this \s-1CCS,\s0 if it can be designated explicitly.
.IP "gr => \s-1BOOLEAN\s0" 4
.IX Item "gr => BOOLEAN"
If true value is set, this \s-1CCS\s0 will be invoked to \s-1GR\s0 using 7\-bit conversion
table.
.IP "ls => \s-1STRING\s0" 4
.IX Item "ls => STRING"
.PD 0
.IP "ss => \s-1STRING\s0" 4
.IX Item "ss => STRING"
.PD
Escape sequence or control character to invoke this \s-1CCS,\s0
if it should be invoked explicitly.
.Sp
If \f(CW\*(C`ls\*(C'\fR is set, this \s-1CCS\s0 will be invoked by locking-shift.
If \f(CW\*(C`ss\*(C'\fR is set, this \s-1CCS\s0 will be invoked by single-shift.
.IP "range => \s-1STRING\s0" 4
.IX Item "range => STRING"
Possible range of encoded bytes.  General value is
\&\f(CW\*(Aq\ex21\-\ex7E\*(Aq\fR, \f(CW\*(Aq\ex20\-\ex7F\*(Aq\fR, \f(CW\*(Aq\exA1\-\exFE\*(Aq\fR or \f(CW\*(Aq\exA0\-\exFF\*(Aq\fR.
This is required for multibyte CCSs to detect broken multibyte sequences.
.RE
.RS 4
.RE
.IP "LineInit => \s-1BOOLEAN\s0" 4
.IX Item "LineInit => BOOLEAN"
If it is true, designation and invokation states will be initialized at
beginning of lines.
.IP "SubChar => \s-1STRING\s0" 4
.IX Item "SubChar => STRING"
Unicode string to be used for substitution character.
.PP
To know more about use of this module,
the source of Encode::ISO2022JP2 may be an example.
.SH "CAVEATS"
.IX Header "CAVEATS"
This module implements small subset of the features defined by
\&\s-1ISO/IEC 2022.\s0
Each encoding recognizes only several predefined designation and invokation
functions.
It can handle limited number of coded character sets.
Variable length multibyte coded character sets aren't supported.
And so on.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
\&\s-1ISO/IEC 2022\s0
\&\fIInformation technology \- Character code structure and extension techniques\fR.
.PP
Encode, Encode::ISO2022::CCS.
